# Audio Routing State Machine Specification (13-State Model)

Below is the state machine diagram representing the lifecycle and status transitions of the Audio Routing mechanism, particularly highlighting how degradation (STT/Translate/TTS latency) and recovery events are resolved via the **Priority Resolver Engine**.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    START(("Start")) --> PENDING["PENDING<br/>Room not started"]
    PENDING -->|config_ready| READY["READY<br/>Languages configured"]
    READY -->|session_starts| BROADCASTING["BROADCASTING<br/>Audio routing is active & healthy"]

    %% Active Streaming States
    subgraph StreamingStates ["Active Streaming States"]
        BROADCASTING
        SPEECH_DELAYED["SPEECH_DELAYED<br/>Whisper speed drop"]
        TRANSLATION_DELAYED["TRANSLATION_DELAYED<br/>NMT latency high"]
        VOICE_DELAYED["VOICE_DELAYED<br/>Speech synthesis slow"]
        STANDARD_VOICE["STANDARD_VOICE<br/>Using generic standard voice"]
        CAPTION_ONLY["CAPTION_ONLY<br/>Plain captions UI delivery"]
    end

    %% Telemetry dynamic prioritization
    StreamingStates -.->|telemetry_state_updated<br/>Calculated by Priority Resolver| StreamingStates

    %% Pause / Resume
    StreamingStates -->|room_pause<br/>(Update Protection active)| PAUSED["PAUSED<br/>Streams suspended"]
    PAUSED -->|room_resume| BROADCASTING

    %% Ending Room
    StreamingStates -->|session_ends / system_disabled| ENDING["ENDING<br/>Winding down streams"]
    PAUSED -->|session_ends / system_disabled| ENDING

    %% Finalization
    ENDING -->|flush_runtime| SAVING_OUTPUTS["SAVING_OUTPUTS<br/>Compiling recordings/transcripts"]
    SAVING_OUTPUTS -->|outputs_linked| COMPLETED["COMPLETED<br/>Terminal Sink State<br/>(Unified Cache Cleaned)"]
    SAVING_OUTPUTS -->|finalization_failed| SAVE_FAILED["SAVE_FAILED<br/>Exhausted local retries"]
    
    SAVE_FAILED -->|flush_runtime<br/>(Recovery Sweep)| SAVING_OUTPUTS
    SAVE_FAILED -->|finalization_abandoned| COMPLETED
    SAVING_OUTPUTS -->|finalization_abandoned| COMPLETED

    COMPLETED --> END(("End"))
```

### State Resolution & Cache Cleanup Rules
1.  **Authoritative State Machine**: The C# Backend orchestrates all transitions and updates PostgreSQL canonical states.
2.  **Unified Telemetry**: Instead of individual direct state transitions, the telemetry processor periodically sweeps Redis volatile indicators and runs the `AudioRoutePriorityResolver` to resolve the current canonical state.
3.  **Update Protection**: Telemetry sweeps are strictly blocked from overwriting the PostgreSQL state if the route status is `PAUSED`.
4.  **Immediate RAM Recovery**: Upon transitioning to the terminal `COMPLETED` state (both on happy-path success and on abandoned failures), the service executes **Unified Redis Cache Cleanup** to instantly delete telemetry and transcript cache keys, ensuring minimum memory foot-print.
